  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🏷️ Sticker Business Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a sticker shop or stationery brand, from Stuck on You to Ashby Stationers."
    },
    "intro": "A good sticker shop name is short enough for a backing card, playful, and says what you sell: a pun on stick and peel, a cute animal, or your own name if you're the artist. Selling stickers on Etsy, at craft fairs or from your own stationery shop? This **sticker business name generator** gives you names in eight styles, from puns to proper stationers, and you can check each one is free before you print your first sheet.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good sticker business names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Peel the Love</strong>: a warm pun on peeling a sticker.</li><li><strong>Stuck on Axolotls</strong>: a pun that also tells people your theme.</li><li><strong>Teeny Penguin Sticker Co.</strong>: a cute animal plus Sticker Co.: clear and friendly.</li><li><strong>Feral Llama Sticker Co.</strong>: funny, for chaotic designs.</li><li><strong>Mochi & Moon Stickers</strong>: soft and aesthetic, for planner stickers.</li><li><strong>Mirror Foil Sticker Works</strong>: modern, and names a finish people search for.</li><li><strong>The Pencil Pot Stationers</strong>: a classic stationer's name if you sell more than stickers.</li><li><strong>Sarah Made a Sticker</strong>: your own name, for an artist-led shop.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How sticker shop names work",
        "content": "<p>Sticker shops sell mostly online and at fairs, so the name has to work as a handle and on a small banner.</p><ul><li><strong>Puns</strong> on stick, peel and vinyl are the classic choice.</li><li><strong>Finish words</strong> help people find you: <em>holo</em>, <em>foil</em>, <em>matte</em>, <em>glossy</em>, <em>washi</em> (decorative Japanese paper tape).</li><li><strong>Kiss-cut and die-cut</strong> are worth knowing: kiss-cut stickers are cut through the sticker but not the backing, so several sit on one sheet; die-cut stickers are cut right through to their shape.</li><li><strong>Your theme</strong> in the name (frogs, plants, cats) brings in people looking for exactly that.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
